  <Document>
    <ParagraphLine TextAlignment="Left" TextType="Normal" BlockID="a7a1412b-97a2-40e0-b7b4-fe6beef4bb17">
      <Normal>
        <Normal>
          <Normal>Ramy and Ahmed, two brothers who come from a rich family. Ahmed the favorite task focused son throws a party celebrating his last achievement in the business world.</Normal>
        </Normal>
      </Normal>
    </ParagraphLine>
    <ParagraphLine TextAlignment="Left" TextType="Normal" BlockID="3145b7c4-6a47-42fd-9653-4c5a4ec0fb08">
      <Normal>
        <Normal>
          <Normal>Ramy, unlike Ahmed, he is the party boy and a trouble maker. He had a rough relationship with his parents and they considered him a shame to the family name.</Normal>
        </Normal>
      </Normal>
    </ParagraphLine>
    <ParagraphLine TextAlignment="Left" TextType="Normal" BlockID="9c8a1215-15b4-4084-8724-7d6915a69ad3">
      <Normal>
        <Normal>
          <Normal>While Ramy's parents hated their son, Ahmed has a soft spot for his brother and as the big brother, he tried his best straighten him up. But Ramy as the trouble maker he is, is just a constant disappointment.</Normal>
        </Normal>
      </Normal>
    </ParagraphLine>
    <ParagraphLine TextAlignment="Left" TextType="Normal" BlockID="de2d95f9-4438-440a-8ec8-c5fda8112939">
      <Normal>
        <Normal>
          <Normal>Ramy's inheritance is running out and he comes to his brother's party to beg him help him start a business.</Normal>
        </Normal>
      </Normal>
    </ParagraphLine>
  </Document>
